{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"x":0.77160493914987061,"w":0.069958845774332645,"y":0.046511627815782663,"t":"1718867188","h":0.008720930389296444,"c":0.5},{"y":0.053779069624731557,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"Test 1","w":0.057613169352213556,"x":0.11728395020043644},{"x":0.11728394439279517,"y":0.097383720794351092,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.29012346903483072,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3"},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","h":0.020366080096529071,"c":1,"x":0.11717780079325119,"w":0.77386769612630224,"y":0.12904351177147777},{"c":1,"w":0.1604938252766927,"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.14811542989978521,"t":"Passage 3 below.","x":0.1172839513854305},{"c":1,"y":0.17728551129482839,"x":0.40054266065119465,"h":0.028106847837198745,"t":"To catch a king","w":0.21762825012207027},{"x":0.13991769318133171,"w":0.73662551879882809,"h":0.017505204860116641,"c":1,"t":"Anna Keay reviews Charles Spencer's book about the hunt for King Charles II","y":0.2223203766893278},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.24691356819542118,"w":0.52263376871744793,"y":0.24263839808521248,"t":"during the English Civil War of the seventeenth century","c":1},{"w":0.33333333333333331,"t":"Charles Spencer's latest book, To Catch a","h":0.016020900088288936,"c":1,"x":0.11728395050898854,"y":0.28197674403711037},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"y":0.29796511613016796,"t":"King, tells us the story of the hunt for King","x":0.11728394862186069,"w":0.34567901611328117},{"c":1,"h":0.019139638076261178,"w":0.3790404001871745,"y":0.31237785577638766,"t":"Charles II in the six weeks after his resounding","x":0.11706416959839772},{"w":0.38065844217936196,"t":"defeat at the Battle of Worcester in September","h":0.016195524146054074,"y":0.33127208487905757,"x":0.11522633436043786,"c":1},{"y":0.34883720916708139,"w":0.35390945434570314,"x":0.11728395584856334,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"1651. And what a story it is. After his father"},{"t":"was executed by the Parliamentarians in 1649,","c":1,"x":0.11934156622835843,"y":0.36482558125909992,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.37242797851562504},{"c":1,"x":0.11522633733853449,"h":0.01472320376914027,"y":0.38221436958060129,"w":0.33333333333333331,"t":"the young Charles II sacrificed one of the"},{"x":0.11522633828140073,"y":0.39811542974892555,"c":1,"w":0.3374485524495443,"t":"very principles his father had died for and","h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"did a deal with the Scots, thereby accepting","h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.41569767428212856,"x":0.11522633903599067,"c":1,"w":0.34979423522949221},{"t":"Presbyterianism* as the national religion in","x":0.11728395549058537,"y":0.43021201389202757,"w":0.34773661295572922,"c":1,"h":0.014555427295159129},{"x":0.11316872491238504,"w":0.35596707661946614,"t":"return for being crowned King of Scots. His","h":0.016195524146054074,"y":0.44758539480684933,"c":1},{"h":0.014565699794126807,"c":1,"y":0.46511627893446339,"t":"arrival in Edinburgh prompted the English","x":0.1152263318572328,"w":0.34156379699707023},{"t":"Parliamentary army to invade Scotland in a","w":0.34567901611328117,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.48110465102745636,"x":0.11728394862392165},{"y":0.49852767951253751,"x":0.11522633186840589,"t":"pre-emptive strike. This was followed by a","w":0.34156379699707029,"h":0.014553715960858749,"c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.11522633453026543,"t":"Scottish invasion of England. The two sides","y":0.51442873984434634,"w":0.35185185750325521},{"h":0.014548579711374909,"y":0.53197674405064999,"x":0.11522634283739155,"w":0.32510286966959634,"c":1,"t":"finally faced one another at Worcester in"},{"c":1,"x":0.11522633831657325,"y":0.54796511614184773,"t":"the west of England in 1651. After being","w":0.32716049194335939,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"w":0.34596883138020834,"y":0.56322018873196078,"t":"comprehensively defeated on the meadows","c":1,"h":0.018246682147957327,"x":0.11509624844210133},{"y":0.5795821853568216,"w":0.3603960418701172,"t":"outside the city by the Parliamentarian army,","h":0.01791729213773019,"x":0.11510740798396303,"c":1},{"x":0.11522633531995012,"w":0.37448560078938803,"y":0.59738372077680668,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"the 21-year-old king found himself the subject","c":1},{"y":0.61482558127205766,"t":"of a national manhunt, with a huge sum","c":1,"x":0.11728394876231665,"h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.31687243143717447},{"x":0.11509167117121506,"y":0.62847709584641465,"t":"offered for his capture. Over the following","w":0.34190836588541668,"h":0.018414973651000865,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.1152263364266408,"t":"six weeks he managed, through a series of","y":0.6481154299252283,"w":0.3395061747233073,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"y":0.66400214145126979,"t":"heart-poundingly close escapes, to evade the","x":0.11511660885456867,"c":1,"h":0.017451165562102799,"w":0.36029731750488281},{"t":"Parliamentarians before seeking refuge in","c":1,"y":0.6786079796027914,"w":0.33576426188151043,"x":0.1150646278262506,"h":0.02046105662279607},{"x":0.11728395490227114,"c":1,"t":"France. For the next nine years, the penniless","y":0.69758539481200321,"w":0.36008229573567707,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"x":0.11508279937838069,"t":"and defeated Charles wandered around Europe","y":0.71097647878711823,"h":0.018893779938858435,"c":1,"w":0.38098612467447918},{"x":0.11728394765411991,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.73110465101239619,"w":0.35185185750325521,"c":1,"t":"with only a small group of loyal supporters."},{"h":0.016195524146054074,"y":0.7629564194893228,"c":1,"w":0.34567901611328122,"x":0.11728394868271058,"t":"Years later, after his restoration as king, the"},{"t":"50-year-old Charles II requested a meeting","y":0.78052325566515213,"w":0.34567901611328122,"h":0.016002068109591039,"x":0.11522633545528303,"c":1},{"w":0.36419754028320317,"h":0.016020900088288936,"c":1,"y":0.28197674403617268,"x":0.51646090056771676,"t":"with the writer and diarist Samuel Pepys. His"},{"c":1,"t":"intention when asking Pepys to commit his","w":0.34773661295572922,"y":0.29796511613048859,"x":0.51440329835500165,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"t":"story to paper was to ensure that this most","y":0.31470041522510694,"x":0.51631041987059756,"w":0.33982030232747407,"h":0.01696136281403271,"c":1},{"x":0.51646090340337003,"y":0.33127208487243709,"c":1,"w":0.34567901611328133,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"extraordinary episode was never forgotten."},{"t":"Over two three-hour sittings, the king related","c":1,"x":0.51646090964363889,"w":0.36008229573567707,"h":0.016003780005537038,"y":0.34883720915402794},{"t":"to him in great detail his personal recollections","c":1,"y":0.36482558118505382,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.37860081990559902,"x":0.5144032934937024},{"y":0.3822143695813478,"w":0.36831275939941399,"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1,"t":"of the six weeks he had spent as a fugitive. As","x":0.51646090414802959},{"y":0.39796783495091281,"h":0.018017816599743663,"t":"the king and secretary settled down (a scene","c":1,"w":0.3562312571207682,"x":0.51427119995762083},{"x":0.51646090605330153,"w":0.35596707661946614,"y":0.41569767428166982,"c":1,"h":0.014534883982160851,"t":"that is surely a gift for a future scriptwriter),"},{"h":0.014536595878106739,"t":"Charles commenced his story: 'After the battle","x":0.5164609032037909,"y":0.43168433448093735,"w":0.37448560078938808,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"was so absolutely lost as to be beyond hope of","h":0.014723203769140047,"w":0.37242797851562504,"x":0.51646090778074361,"y":0.44905771517594362},{"y":0.46511627892012486,"w":0.35596707661946614,"h":0.016038020171040723,"t":"recovery, I began to think of the best way of","c":1,"x":0.51440329289304942},{"h":0.015925295642183257,"c":1,"y":0.48169458468646464,"t":"saving myself.'","x":0.51427058458513519,"w":0.12600135803222656},{"y":0.5144287398437779,"t":"One of the joys of Spencer's book, a result not","c":1,"w":0.37242797851562504,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.51646090777939735},{"x":0.51646091152107432,"c":1,"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.53197674407789763,"t":"least of its use of Charles Il's own narrative","w":0.34773661295572911},{"t":"as well as those of his supporters, is just how","y":0.54796511612976329,"x":0.51646090964897018,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"w":0.36008229573567718},{"h":0.016043156420524562,"c":1,"x":0.51646090319123839,"w":0.37448560078938797,"t":"close the reader gets to the action. The day-by-","y":0.56389870418300914},{"y":0.57979976439999548,"t":"day retelling of the fugitives' doings provides","c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.51646091402467331,"w":0.364197514851888},{"y":0.59738372114834681,"w":0.37037035624186199,"x":0.51646091380293735,"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"t":"delicious details: the cutting of the king's long"},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"x":0.51646090319821514,"y":0.6148255812604333,"t":"hair with agricultural shears, the use of walnut","w":0.37448560078938808},{"w":0.37860081990559902,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.51440329356182624,"t":"leaves to dye his pale skin, and the day Charles","y":0.63074204921521537},{"x":0.51440329821323605,"w":0.37654319763183597,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"spent lying on a branch of the great oak tree in","y":0.64811542992589244},{"t":"Boscobel Wood as the Parliamentary soldiers","x":0.5164609005305103,"w":0.36419754028320317,"h":0.014534883982160851,"y":0.66424418591146495,"c":1},{"t":"scoured the forest floor below. Spencer draws","x":0.51631150547296556,"y":0.67953303759501971,"h":0.017387412040899108,"w":0.364496332804362,"c":1},{"y":0.69708000822363136,"t":"out both the humour - such as the preposterous","c":1,"w":0.3808611043294271,"h":0.015701598357255708,"x":0.51635189128759917},{"c":1,"t":"refusal of Charles's friend Henry Wilmot","h":0.019535015272448275,"x":0.51423523827610929,"y":0.71104400960118752,"w":0.33374242146809896},{"t":"to adopt disguise on the grounds that it was","c":1,"x":0.51851851652876579,"y":0.73110465102675204,"w":0.34567901611328122,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"c":1,"t":"beneath his dignity - and the emotional tension","x":0.51646090228435737,"h":0.016026036337772775,"w":0.38065844217936196,"y":0.74705535914894838},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"x":0.51851852197481629,"y":0.76442873987007798,"w":0.33744855244954419,"t":"when the secret of the king's presence was"},{"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"cautiously revealed to his supporters.","x":0.51851851945965222,"y":0.78052325567364844,"w":0.29835390726725264},{"t":"* Presbyterianism: part of the reformed Protestant religion","x":0.11717720183275067,"w":0.32530057271321616,"c":1,"y":0.84588627276101525,"h":0.013191253473396447},{"w":0.024691357612609863,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.11728395072044402,"t":"24","y":0.86773255795657411},{"y":0.95314993691982619,"x":0.66984496081179823,"h":0.035152653221247165,"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30619837443033859}]}